            0.109
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "2.3.1 Why do eukaryotic cells need these organelles?"
            }
          ],
          "level": 2
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 1,
          "bbox": [
            0.223,
            0.111,
            0.888,
            0.147
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Eukaryotic cells carry out various life processes in different cell organelles independently at the same time."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 2,
          "bbox": [
            0.223,
            0.148,
            0.891,
            0.219
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Cell organelles help in building new materials, removing waste, and providing energy to the cell. They work together to perform all functions of a cell. In other words, a cell is like a tiny living factory, with each of its part doing a specific job."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 3,
          "bbox": [
            0.253,
            0.226,
            0.819,
            0.245
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Let us explore these specialised structures present inside a cell."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "image",
          "index": 4,
          "bbox": [
            0.03,
            0.221,
            0.221,
            0.622
          ],
          "content": [
            {
